            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "awesome in tummy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the same recipe that I got years ago from my mom only her's made more. She used 2c sour cream, 2c mayo, 1T parsley, 1T dried onion, 1T dill weed or seeds and 1T beau monde. Same ingredients, larger amount. It is really good as a dip for fresh veggies too! Thanks Tish!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MsHissy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a very flavorful dip, and it doesn't last long at our house. Beau Monde Seasoning is sometimes hard to find at the grocery store, so I looked at the ingredients and came up with my own mix. 1 teaspoon salt 0.25 teaspoon white granulated sugar 2 teaspoons onion powder 2 teaspoons celery seed Mix well, Store in an airtight container at room temperature.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-16T23:25:22.569Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CabHop"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This dip looks good although I would exclude mayo account an aversion to it. My mother would use Beau Monde seasoning mixed into softened cream cheese to stuff celery sticks for special occasion meals.",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-27T17:50:37.154Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debra K Totten Gauthier"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have used the Beau Monde Dip for years!!! Now days, I add plain yogurt to cut the fats, but still use mayo and sour cream, just less of it. It is a favorite either way and I will always love it !!! Something about that spice, just can't be beat!!",
            "datePublished": "2022-06-18T02:11:48.391Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "5flipgirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Everyone loved this including the kids! I forgot to add the onions and it still turned out really good. I added some dried beef to it and I used a sweet hawaiian bread bowl to serve it in and ripped up extra sweet rolls. I also doubled the recipe. It was so good and addicting everyone couldn't stop eating it.",
            "datePublished": "2009-01-06T16:02:30.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've been making this dip for over 30 years. Although we refer to it as dill dip. I typically hollow out a loaf of round bread, fill it with the dip and serve it with the bread pieces I pulled out, fresh raw vegetables and chips. I've found that it really needs to chill overnight in fridge for the favor to really come out.",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-12T15:12:58.065Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Soup Loving Nicole"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made as written and this was really good. The key is to make the dip and let it sit for at least 24 hours. The seasoning is a bit difficult to find these day. I bought mine online and then recreated it so that I could have it on hand at all times. It makes a great rub for chicken too.",
            "datePublished": "2024-03-26T01:55:46.711Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "johnsbaby"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I too have served this dip at every Christmas, also adding chipped ham or chipped beef, and serving in a round rye bowl and breaking the remainder of rye and also pumpernickle. First time I ever made it I mistakenly used miracle whip (ouch) you must use real mayo for this recipe, and if you do not like dill, cut it out completely. Either way this is a traditional recipe in my family. Note: to fill a round rye or round pumpernickle bread bowl, you deff need to double the recipe. I place the bread bowl center of large platter and surround with Dark pumpernickle and light rye broken bread chunks.",
            "datePublished": "2006-12-20T17:58:52.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SpiffyDill6979"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used fresh parsley but other than that I follow the recipe as written. It is delicious with potato chips, but I also like to use this to dip chicken breasts before covering them in bread crumbs and baking. An extra layer flavor!",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-03T16:50:05.289Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ladabeehn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mom always made this. She would hollow out a Pumpernickle or Rye bread. Chop up another loaf or 2 for dipping. Yummy!! My childhood favorite. Now I make it and people rave!! Also great with veggies.",
            "datePublished": "2025-09-06T16:23:57.325Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jeff Vino"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm a huge dill fan. I came across this when I searched for dill dip and beau monde. I would say to season to taste because the beau monde makes this dip. The recipe is the same that was passed down to me but I add dill and beau monde until it tastes just rate. I usually eat it with vegetables but one reviewer said they love it with ruffles, which was exactly what I was eating when I saw this recipe, ruffles and dill dip.",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-29T05:34:02.380Z"
